  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000120562,
      "SummaryText": "Nouryon Surface Chemistry LLC owns and operates a specialty chemical manufacturing facility at 485 Cedar Springs Road, Rowan County, Salisbury, North Carolina.  This facility is surrounded by local businesses and residences.  Approximately 109 persons from the surrounding community are employed full-time by Nouryon Surface Chemistry LLC.\n\nIt is the policy of Nouryon Surface Chemistry LLC to meet all requirements established by applicable safety, health, and environmental regulations.  The Salisbury facility has always put safety first.  \n\nNouryon Surface Chemistry LLC stores the following RMP-applicable compounds on-site in quantities that exceed the applicable threshold quantities:  acrylonitrile (CAS No. 107-13-1), sulfur trioxide (CAS No. 7446-11-9), and vinyl acetate (CAS No. 108-05-4).  \n\nNouryon Surface Chemistry LLC's Salisbury site currently maintains an OSHA Process Safety Management (PSM) program for the aforementioned compounds.  Nouryon Surface Chemistry LLC has previously analyzed hazards associated with these processes and developed emergency response plans for responding to incidents involving these compounds.  \n\nNouryon Surface Chemistry LLC has worked to maintain a safe environment for their employees and the surrounding community.  The facility obtained the American Chemistry Council's Responsible Care (RC)14001 certification in 2010 and was recertified on 5/28/15.  (The facility is also certified to ISO 9000.)\n\nNouryon Surface Chemistry LLC's Salisbury site has established an emergency response program detailing specific actions to be taken in the event an incident involving the regulated compounds occurs.  The facility has coordinated training and emergency response activities with Rowan County Emergency Management and the Salisbury Fire Department."
    }
  ]
